WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.730
Line 5 waits for search(q).

2
00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:04.760
Line 6 calls render(items).

3
00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:07.800
We set breakpoints on line 6.

4
00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:11.730
A line breakpoint on line 6 pauses twice.

5
00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:13.940
Pause 1: q is react.

6
00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:18.800
Pause 2: q is re, so the list shows re results.

7
00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:24.240
Now add a condition to line 6: q !== input.value.

8
00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:26.770
Condition false means no pause.

9
00:00:26.770 --> 00:00:30.800
Condition true pauses on the stale re response.

10
00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:37.000
The Call Stack shows onInput app.js:6, then await, then onInput app.js:5.

11
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:42.800
The frames below await show the call that started the wait.

12
00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:47.350
A logpoint on line 6 prints q and input.value.

13
00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:51.960
The Console shows render react react, then render re react.

14
00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:53.800
The page never pauses.

15
00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:56.970
Add vendor/events.js to the ignore list.

16
00:00:56.970 --> 00:00:59.270
Ignore list off: five frames.

17
00:00:59.270 --> 00:01:04.800
Ignore list on: only your own frames stay in the Call Stack.
